{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/postHog(projectToken:host:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" makes an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") for your PostHog project in one call. It checks"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the project token and the host, posts to the host’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/batch\/"},{"type":"text","text":" with a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"splits each batch to PostHog’s limits ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). A batch with no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record the encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. It retries no response, a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"5xx, 408 and 429, and drops and reports any other status. The project token goes in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the body, so no header field is needed, and no trace context is sent. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this module out; import it on its own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each record becomes an anonymous event. Its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"text":" is the record’s session, from the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sessions enricher, also sent as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$session_id"},{"text":"; a record with no session is sent under its own","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record identifier. Its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uuid"},{"text":" is the record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps. Every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event carries ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$process_person_profile: false"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$geoip_disable: true"},{"text":". The record’s vendor","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identifier and trace context aren’t sent, and the standard context is sent as PostHog’s own","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"properties (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_version"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device_model"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os_name"},{"text":" and the like).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is made with. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals, and a property whose name starts with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$"},{"type":"text","text":" or is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is left out and logged. A record the encoder can’t write is left out and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe, one whose event name starts with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one whose event isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", one holding a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp has no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ISO 8601 form (NaN, infinite, or more than "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int64.max"},{"type":"text","text":" milliseconds from 1970), and one too large"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for PostHog’s event limit. The destination reports each as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reason is a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogEncodingError"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To send to TraffluentCollector, use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorBatchEncoder"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CollectorEncoding"},{"text":")","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import HTTPDestinations","import PostHogEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let postHog = try HTTPDestination.postHog(","    projectToken: projectToken,","    host: postHogHost,  \/\/ https:\/\/us.i.posthog.com, https:\/\/eu.i.posthog.com or your own","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: postHog)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what PostHog receives, and why, in more detail."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/posthogencoding"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to PostHog Cloud or a self-hosted PostHog through its batch capture API."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sending-to-PostHog","title":"Sending to PostHog","identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/postHog(projectToken:host:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/postHog(projectToken:host:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogSetupError"]},{"anchor":"Encoding-batches","title":"Encoding batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder"]},{"anchor":"Records-left-out","title":"Records left out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogEncodingError"]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"PostHogEncoding","roleHeading":"Framework","symbolKind":"module","title":"PostHogEncoding","modules":[{"name":"PostHogEncoding"}],"role":"collection"},"references":{"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/choosingdestinations":{"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Choosing Destinations"}],"title":"Choosing Destinations","type":"link"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/BatchEncoder":{"role":"symbol","title":"BatchEncoder","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/batchencoder","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What turns a batch of records into the requests "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" sends."}]},"doc://PostHogEncoding/documentation/PostHogEncoding":{"type":"topic","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to PostHog Cloud or a self-hosted PostHog through its batch capture API."}],"title":"PostHogEncoding","url":"\/documentation\/posthogencoding"},"doc://PostHogEncoding/documentation/PostHogEncoding/PostHogBatchEncoder/batchLimit":{"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"batchLimit","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchLimit","preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"title":"batchLimit","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/posthogencoding\/posthogbatchencoder\/batchlimit","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"PostHog’s limits on one request: 10,000,000 bytes of body and 1,000,000 bytes of one event,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with no limit on the count of events."}]},"doc://PostHogEncoding/documentation/PostHogEncoding/PostHogBatchEncoder":{"role":"symbol","title":"PostHogBatchEncoder","url":"\/documentation\/posthogencoding\/postho